# settings-home: the real main screen with the firmware's real Ajustes window
# open over it. The path is the firmware's own:
# main_screen_action(ACTION_APP_SETTINGS) -> src/main_screen.c
# (main_screen_start_app) -> src/dialog.c (dialog_construct/dialog_init) ->
# src/dialog_settings.c (the whole grid: date/time, clock, backlight, info,
# audio, spectrum, waterfall, operations, appearance and the action dropdowns).
#
# The dialog opens on its first group, which after the utility ordering of
# issue #109 is Operation, so the fixture jumps to the Clock group the way the
# user does: `buttons_press(3)` presses the page 1 "Clock" tab, which calls
# settings_goto() (scroll + focus). The render therefore shows the date/time and
# clock rows plus the tab bar, the same screen this fixture has always measured
# (src/screens.c, scenario_settle, codifies that the date row is on screen).
# Deterministic: the date/time fields read the harness' fixed clock, not the
# host's (tools/ui_harness/CMakeLists.txt links with `--wrap=time`).

name settings-home
screen settings-home

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
